BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mary Oliver: Saved by the Beauty of the World
DTSTART:20260727T224500Z
DTEND:20260728T003500Z
DTSTAMP:20260727T224500Z
UID:q38kOiXrIJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nMary Oliver – best-selling poet
  and Pulitzer Prize-winner\; lover of dogs and long walks in the woods\; q
 ueer and out\, but intensely private. Her poems inspire liberals and conse
 rvatives\, atheists and believers\, naturalists and urbanites. If poetry h
 ad a pop icon\, Mary Oliver would be it. Featuring poems read by Helena Bo
 nham Carter\, Steve Buscemi\, Stephen Colbert\, Lucy Dacus\, Jesse Welles\
 , and Oprah Winfrey.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/mary-olive
 r-saved-by-the-beauty-of-the-world\n\nEstimated start: 16:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seattle 48 Hour Film Project
DTSTART:20260728T013000Z
DTEND:20260728T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20260728T013000Z
UID:Hqf66nKNOq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nPresented by CREATE48 Media Netwo
 rk. Watch the world premieres of films created in just 48 hours by Seattl
 e filmmakers. The 2026 Seattle 48 Hour Film Project showcases original sho
 rt films spanning every genre\, celebrating creativity\, collaboration\, a
 nd the incredible challenge of making a movie from script to screen in one
  weekend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-48-hour-film-
 project\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
